---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Matt Hurley - Educator & Software Developer" 
  description="Educator-led software development focused on practical systems, privacy-first principles, and maintainable architecture."
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero">
      <img src="/logo.PNG" alt="Matt Hurley" class="hero-logo">
    </div>
    
    <div class="intro">
      <h1>Matt Hurley</h1>
      <p>
        Educator and software developer building practical, privacy-first systems 
        that address real constraints and serve real users.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Educator-Led Development</h2>
      <p>
        Software development informed by years of teaching, leadership, and systems thinking. 
        Each project reflects a commitment to clarity, maintainability, and ethical design—
        prioritizing user needs and operational realities over technical novelty.
      </p>
      <p>
        The projects documented here are extensions of problem-solving in education contexts, 
        personal infrastructure, and independent exploration. They are not commercial offerings, 
        but reflections of how thoughtful design can serve specific needs effectively.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="stats-section">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-number">5+</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Active Projects</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-number">100%</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Privacy-First</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-number">Open</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Source</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <a href="/projects" class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">💼</div>
          <h3>Projects</h3>
          <p>Detailed case studies of independent software systems, including architecture decisions, constraints, and real-world impact.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/writing" class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">✍️</div>
          <h3>Writing</h3>
          <p>Reflections on building software in education, privacy and governance, and lessons learned from real deployments.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/about" class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">👤</div>
          <h3>About</h3>
          <p>Background, philosophy, and approach to software development informed by education leadership.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/contact" class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">📧</div>
          <h3>Contact</h3>
          <p>Get in touch via email or GitHub to discuss projects, collaboration, or educational technology.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
